---
description: Loading indicator pattern (DialogUtils)
alwaysApply: true
---
 Loading indicator pattern (DialogUtils):

  When implementing async operations with a loading dialog:

  - Open loading without await and keep the returned handle:
      LoadingDialog? loading;
      if (mounted) {
        loading = DialogUtils.openLoading(context, message: 'İşlem yapılıyor...');
      }
    (DialogUtils.openLoadingProgress works the same way.)

  - Always close the loading through the handle BEFORE showing info/error dialogs:
      loading?.close();
    Never close it with Navigator.pop: while the loading is open a notification
    may push a page (e.g. a chat) on top, and pop would close that page instead.
    close() removes only the loading dialog, needs no context or mounted check
    and is safe to call more than once.

  - If the page (or dialog) closes itself when the work is done, use
      DialogUtils.closeOwnRoute(context);            // or (context, result)
    instead of Navigator.pop: for the same reason it removes only its own route.

  - Wrap async work in try / catch / finally:
    - In try: perform the operation.
    - On success:
        - close loading (loading?.close())
        - show info dialog (DialogUtils.openInfo)
        - refresh data/state if needed.
    - On error:
        - close loading (loading?.close())
        - show error dialog (DialogUtils.openError)
    - In finally:
        - close loading too if the try has early returns
        - reset local busy flags with setState if mounted.

  - Always use mounted checks before:
    - opening dialogs
    - calling setState
    - using context-dependent APIs.
